# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# NexusAI Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Required ──
# Hugging Face Inference API token
# Get one free at: https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens
HF_TOKEN=hf_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Optional: Web Search ──
# Tavily API key for real-time web search (free tier: 1000 searches/month)
# Get one at: https://tavily.com
TAVILY_API_KEY=tvly-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Optional: Cloud Self-Improvement Cache ──
# Vercel KV (Redis) for storing self-improved responses in the cloud.
# This enables cross-session learning — ALL users benefit from past improvements.
# Without this, self-analysis still works (auto-corrects responses), but improved
# versions aren't cached for future queries.
#
# How to set up (FREE on Vercel):
# 1. Go to your Vercel project → Storage tab
# 2. Click "Create Database" → Select "KV (Redis)"
# 3. Choose the Free plan (256MB storage, 3000 requests/day)
# 4. Link it to your project
# 5. Vercel will auto-add KV_REST_URL and KV_REST_TOKEN to your env vars
#
# Then install the package:
#   npm install @vercel/kv
#
# KV_REST_URL and KV_REST_TOKEN are auto-set by Vercel KV integration.
# You only need to install @vercel/kv as a dependency.
KV_REST_URL=
KV_REST_TOKEN=
